## Proposed Changes

### 1. Database Schema (Laravel)

We only need three clean tables to manage this workflow:

#### `courses` (To manage what courses are displayed and their prices)
*   `id` (BIGINT, PK, Auto Increment)
*   `title` (VARCHAR)
*   `slug` (VARCHAR, Unique)
*   `description` (TEXT)
*   `price` (DECIMAL 10,2)
*   `whatsapp_group_link` (VARCHAR, Nullable) - The fallback invite link.
*   `is_active` (BOOLEAN, Default: true)
*   `timestamps`

#### `course_registrations` (To store student details and links)
*   `id` (BIGINT, PK, Auto Increment)
*   `course_id` (FOREIGN KEY -> `courses.id`)
*   `name` (VARCHAR)
*   `email` (VARCHAR)
*   `whatsapp_number` (VARCHAR)
*   `company_name` (VARCHAR, Nullable)
*   `whatsapp_invite_link` (VARCHAR, Nullable) - Specific link assigned manually or via API.
*   `status` (ENUM: 'pending', 'completed')
*   `timestamps`

#### `transactions` (To track Xendit payments)
*   `id` (BIGINT, PK, Auto Increment)
*   `registration_id` (FOREIGN KEY -> `course_registrations.id`, Cascade on delete)
*   `invoice_number` (VARCHAR, Unique)
*   `amount` (DECIMAL 10,2)
*   `status` (ENUM: 'pending', 'paid', 'expired', 'failed')
*   `xendit_invoice_id` (VARCHAR, Nullable)
*   `payment_url` (VARCHAR, Nullable)
*   `paid_at` (TIMESTAMP, Nullable)
*   `timestamps`

---

### 2. Backend API Endpoint Details

#### Public Course Catalog
*   `GET /api/courses` - Fetch courses for listing.
*   `GET /api/courses/{slug}` - Fetch specific course.

#### Checkout & Payments
*   `POST /api/course-registrations` - Creates registration and transaction, calls Xendit Invoice, and returns `payment_url`.
*   `GET /api/transactions/status/{invoice_number}` - Returns transaction status and the registration-specific `whatsapp_invite_link` (falling back to course `whatsapp_group_link` if empty).
*   `POST /api/webhooks/xendit` - Public callback endpoint that updates status and marks registration as `'completed'`.

#### Admin/API Management (Protected by Sanctum or API Token)
*   `GET/POST/PUT/DELETE /api/courses` - Admin management of courses.
*   `GET /api/admin/registrations` - List registrations (leads) showing details and payment statuses.
*   `PATCH /api/admin/registrations/{id}/whatsapp-link` - Set or override the WhatsApp invite link for a specific registration (accessible via admin UI or programmatically by external tools using an API token).

---

### 3. Frontend Next.js Pages

#### Course Section
*   `/courses` - Course selection grid.
*   `/courses/[slug]` - Course info with a "Daftar & Bayar" form.
*   `/checkout/success?invoice_number=INV-xxx` - Polling page. When paid:
    *   If `whatsapp_invite_link` is present, render the "Gabung Grup WhatsApp" button.
    *   If no link is available yet, display: *"Pembayaran Berhasil! PIC kami sedang memproses link WhatsApp Anda. Halaman ini akan terupdate otomatis, atau Anda akan dihubungi langsung."*

#### Admin CMS Workspace
*   `/admin/registrations` - Leads dashboard showing transaction status and an **"Assign WhatsApp Link"** input field next to each entry to allow manual inputs.

